WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:03.067
-Dorinda, we have
so much to talk about.

00:00:03.067 --> 00:00:05.334
-So much to talk about.
-You know I'm a fan of yours.

00:00:05.334 --> 00:00:06.601
-I hear your wife is, as well.

00:00:06.601 --> 00:00:08.701
-Nancy. The Fallon family
loves Dorinda.

00:00:08.701 --> 00:00:10.567
-I love Nancy.
-Oh, we love you so much.

00:00:10.567 --> 00:00:13.167
-Are you shocked or surprised
ever when a celebrity is like,

00:00:13.167 --> 00:00:14.534
"I'm a big fan of yours"?

00:00:14.534 --> 00:00:16.200
Because I know there are
some famous ones out there.

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:17.567
Sarah Paulson.
-Yes, love her.

00:00:17.567 --> 00:00:19.667
-Lady Gaga loves you.
-Yes.

00:00:19.667 --> 00:00:21.434
-Rihanna.

00:00:21.434 --> 00:00:23.300
-She wants to come
to the Berkshires.

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:26.033
-I have this. She wants
to come to the Berkshires.

00:00:26.033 --> 00:00:27.334
You posted this.

00:00:27.334 --> 00:00:29.667
And then look, down here,
badgalriri says,

00:00:29.667 --> 00:00:32.267
"I wanna come over."

00:00:32.267 --> 00:00:34.300
-Riri --
She can bring the baby now.

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:35.968
-She can bring the baby.
-It's so easy.

00:00:35.968 --> 00:00:38.033
It's such a baby-friendly place.
-It is?

00:00:38.033 --> 00:00:39.367
Yeah, I want to come by.

00:00:39.367 --> 00:00:40.734
So Rihanna
hasn't been there yet?

00:00:40.734 --> 00:00:42.534
-She hasn't been there yet.
-Rihanna, open invitation.

00:00:42.534 --> 00:00:44.033
-But I've got to tell you
a funny story.

00:00:44.033 --> 00:00:46.200
So, when I called my parents,

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:48.367
who everyone has seen on TV,
and they're older now.

00:00:48.367 --> 00:00:50.267
-Yeah.
-They live in the Berkshires.

00:00:50.267 --> 00:00:52.567
I called up and I said,
"Hey, Mom. Guess what."

00:00:52.567 --> 00:00:54.667
"Hey, John,
your daughter's on the phone!"

00:00:54.667 --> 00:00:55.934
So, of course, it's 20 minutes.

00:00:55.934 --> 00:00:57.767
They make it on the phone.
They pick up.

00:00:57.767 --> 00:00:59.267
"Yeah, what's going on?
Everything okay?

00:00:59.267 --> 00:01:02.601
"Yeah, everything's -- I'm going
to be on 'The Tonight Show.'"

00:01:02.601 --> 00:01:05.667
"John, your daughter's
gonna be on 'Johnny Carson'!"

00:01:05.667 --> 00:01:07.767
[ Laughter ]

00:01:07.767 --> 00:01:09.167
[ Applause ]

00:01:09.167 --> 00:01:11.767
And I just couldn't
break it to them.

00:01:11.767 --> 00:01:14.734
-[As Carson] "I'm very excited
that you're here tonight.

00:01:14.734 --> 00:01:16.100
It's unbelievable."

00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:18.868
-It just cracked me up.
-[Normal voice] They're like,

00:01:18.868 --> 00:01:20.133
"What is going on right now?!"

00:01:20.133 --> 00:01:21.701
-Oh, they're gonna be so asleep.

00:01:21.701 --> 00:01:23.100
[ Laughter ]

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:24.801
-You've had some of
the most iconic lines

00:01:24.801 --> 00:01:26.133
in "Housewives" history.

00:01:26.133 --> 00:01:27.701
I want to show
a couple of these.

00:01:27.701 --> 00:01:29.834
Because these were memes
that went around online.

00:01:29.834 --> 00:01:31.934
-Uh-oh.
-No.

00:01:31.934 --> 00:01:33.501
I just loved you
right after this.

00:01:33.501 --> 00:01:36.934
You said, "I decorated.
I cooked. I made it nice."

00:01:36.934 --> 00:01:38.567
[ Laughter ]
"I made it nice."

00:01:38.567 --> 00:01:39.868
-And that's a sentiment

00:01:39.868 --> 00:01:42.000
that all women feel,
like, in the world, you know?

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:43.300
And I'm going to tell you --

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:44.934
Because these girls
were acting terribly

00:01:44.934 --> 00:01:46.834
and not appreciating
anything I was doing.

00:01:46.834 --> 00:01:48.033
-Yeah, exactly.
-And I was fed up.

00:01:48.033 --> 00:01:50.100
-Yeah, and you gotta tell them
what's up!

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:52.234
-I cooked, I cleaned,
I made it nice!

00:01:52.234 --> 00:01:54.200
-"I made it nice!" Come on.

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:58.000
-We've all felt like that.
-This one made me laugh.

00:01:58.000 --> 00:01:59.901
"Martinis are like breasts.

00:01:59.901 --> 00:02:02.601
Two are great.
Three are too many."

00:02:02.601 --> 00:02:04.300
-We've seen it on TV.

00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:06.267
Dorinda on three martinis
isn't so good.

00:02:06.267 --> 00:02:08.634
I'm great at two,
not so great at three.

00:02:08.634 --> 00:02:11.267
-You're good TV at three,
though.

00:02:11.267 --> 00:02:15.667
This one went uber-viral
during the pandemic.

00:02:15.667 --> 00:02:17.367
Everyone just sent this around.

00:02:17.367 --> 00:02:19.067
Someone said, "How you doing?"

00:02:19.067 --> 00:02:21.267
You go, "I'll tell you
how I'm doing. Not well..."

00:02:21.267 --> 00:02:24.334
-Bitch!
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:02:24.334 --> 00:02:26.901
-And I said it
to Candace Bushnell.

00:02:26.901 --> 00:02:28.968
That was the biggest joke of it.

00:02:28.968 --> 00:02:31.734
But let me tell you
something about that.

00:02:31.734 --> 00:02:33.667
I made a lot of money on mugs
off of that one

00:02:33.667 --> 00:02:35.734
during the pandemic.
-Mugs? Oh, really?

00:02:35.734 --> 00:02:37.968
-I mean, I could not
keep them in stock.

00:02:37.968 --> 00:02:40.133
Mugs, totes, and sweatshirts.

00:02:40.133 --> 00:02:41.868
I couldn't pack that [bleep]
fast enough.

00:02:41.868 --> 00:02:43.100
Oh, you can't swear.

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:45.200
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:49.033
-Mom! Hey, Mom, Dad, mute the --
mute the TV for a second.

00:02:49.033 --> 00:02:51.267
-I couldn't pack that stuff
fast enough.

00:02:51.267 --> 00:02:53.300
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:02:53.300 --> 00:02:56.467
-When you do stuff like this,
did you know that

00:02:56.467 --> 00:02:59.634
you wanted to be on TV
and wanted to be a housewife?

00:02:59.634 --> 00:03:02.300
-No.
-You didn't? You didn't know?

00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:04.067
-It was never
in my thought process.

00:03:04.067 --> 00:03:07.334
I really thought that sort of
Hannah would go to college,

00:03:07.334 --> 00:03:08.534
and Richard and I would live

00:03:08.534 --> 00:03:10.400
happily ever after
in the Berkshires.

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:12.767
Kind of live in London
and New York

00:03:12.767 --> 00:03:15.300
and do that sort of
"after kids are gone" thing.

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:16.868
But everything changed.

00:03:16.868 --> 00:03:19.567
And then, you know, I got a call
if I was interested.

00:03:19.567 --> 00:03:22.467
And I met with people.
And a month later, I was on.

00:03:22.467 --> 00:03:24.133
You want to hear
a funny story, Jimmy?

00:03:24.133 --> 00:03:26.167
-Of course.
-Here I go again.

00:03:26.167 --> 00:03:27.534
I'll tell you something.

00:03:27.534 --> 00:03:29.601
I remember I was filming
with Ramona Singer,

00:03:29.601 --> 00:03:30.968
my first scene in the Hamptons.

00:03:30.968 --> 00:03:32.133
-Love her.
-Yep.

00:03:32.133 --> 00:03:33.767
And I'm going to
tell you something.

00:03:33.767 --> 00:03:36.100
The camera came around
the corner, and I thought,

00:03:36.100 --> 00:03:39.968
"Hm, I like the camera, and
I think the camera likes me."

00:03:39.968 --> 00:03:41.334
-You felt it?!
-I felt it.

00:03:41.334 --> 00:03:43.868
-You felt it right there.
-And from there on, I was like,

00:03:43.868 --> 00:03:46.667
"This works for me."
-Yeah, you're a star.

00:03:46.667 --> 00:03:48.767
-I don't know if I was a star,
but I liked the whole banter.

00:03:48.767 --> 00:03:51.000
-You are fantastic,
and you're one of my favorites.

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:52.834
I'm so happy
that you're on the show.

00:03:52.834 --> 00:03:54.300
-Thank you.
-You're so good.

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:56.300
I want to show a clip.
Here's Dorinda Medley

00:03:56.300 --> 00:03:58.400
In "The Real Housewives
Ultimate Girls Trip:

00:03:58.400 --> 00:03:59.734
Ex-Wives Club."

00:03:59.734 --> 00:04:02.167
You can watch this one.
Take a look.

00:04:02.167 --> 00:04:03.501
-There was food in the bedrooms.

00:04:03.501 --> 00:04:05.300
I don't like food
in the bedrooms.

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:10.000
-You know what?
Marco brought us yogurts.

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:12.234
-Fruit, yogurt.

00:04:12.234 --> 00:04:13.701
[ Indistinct conversations ]

00:04:13.701 --> 00:04:15.567
-I just don't do food --
-I agree with you.

00:04:15.567 --> 00:04:17.501
-'Cause you know what?
-You should know.

00:04:17.501 --> 00:04:20.534
-I'm so petrified of mice
and things.

00:04:20.534 --> 00:04:22.300
-I actually have that policy
at my house.

00:04:22.300 --> 00:04:24.634
-It says it on the plaque.
"Clear liquid."

00:04:24.634 --> 00:04:26.667
Everyone has a plaque
in their room.

00:04:26.667 --> 00:04:28.934
-There's so much going on
in that room...

00:04:28.934 --> 00:04:30.434
hanging off the ceiling.
-Let me get the plaque.

00:04:30.434 --> 00:04:32.234
-Oh, no, I got it.
I don't need the plaque.

00:04:32.234 --> 00:04:33.367
-I'll get the plaque.

00:04:33.367 --> 00:04:34.634
-I don't need the plaque,
Dorinda. I got it.

00:04:34.634 --> 00:04:36.000
No food in the room.

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:38.868
She's so worried
about rats and mice.

00:04:38.868 --> 00:04:41.534
Why did she put cupcakes
in our room?

00:04:41.534 --> 00:04:43.133
-Dorinda Medley, everybody.

00:04:43.133 --> 00:04:45.400
Catch new episodes of
"The Real Housewives

00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:48.200
Ultimate Girls Trip:
Ex-Wives Club,"

00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:49.467
only on Peacock.

